  "problem": "Ted plays soccer. The following table shows the ages and corresponding weights of five of Ted's teammates.   \n\n| **Age (years)** | **$10$** | **$11$** | **$12$** | **$13$** | **$14$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight (kg)** | $30$ | $40$ | $40$ | $50$ | $60$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?",
  "worked_solution": "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (age) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (weight) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/135eafa5842b7def7177292f8651834aafb8b4ab446afb676976f3fa50850e5d.png)",
